### Integrations homework: ready-made requests
### Works with the REST Client extension for VS Code (humao.rest-client). In Postman or Bruno,
### create the same requests by hand: method, URL, headers and body are shown below.
### Fill in the four values below. Never commit a real secret.

@tenantId = <your tenant id>
@clientId = <your Entra application (client) id>
@clientSecret = <your client secret>
@environmentName = <your sandbox name, for example sandbox>

@scope = https://api.businesscentral.dynamics.com/.default
@baseUri = https://api.businesscentral.dynamics.com/v2.0/{{tenantId}}/{{environmentName}}

### 1. Get a token (client credentials). A 401 here means tenant id, secret or scope is wrong.

# @name auth
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials
&client_id={{clientId}}
&client_secret={{clientSecret}}
&scope={{scope}}

### Token and the first company id, reused by the requests below

@accessHeader = Bearer {{auth.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 2. Standard API v2.0: list companies. A 401 with a good token means the app is not Enabled on the
### Microsoft Entra Applications page. A 403 means no permission sets or no admin consent.

# @name companies
GET {{baseUri}}/api/v2.0/companies HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{accessHeader}}

###

@companyId = {{companies.response.body.value.[0].id}}

### 3. Custom API page from the sample app: list car brands

# @name carBrands
GET {{baseUri}}/api/growthlab/workshop/v1.0/companies({{companyId}})/carBrands HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{accessHeader}}

### Stretch: only rows changed since a date (delta load)

GET {{baseUri}}/api/growthlab/workshop/v1.0/companies({{companyId}})/carBrands?$filter=lastModifiedDateTime gt 2026-11-01T00:00:00Z HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{accessHeader}}

### Stretch: create a car brand, then read it back with request 3

POST {{baseUri}}/api/growthlab/workshop/v1.0/companies({{companyId}})/carBrands HTTP/1.1
Authorization: {{accessHeader}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "TEST01",
  "name": "Test brand",
  "countryRegionCode": "GB",
  "foundedYear": 2026,
  "active": true
}
